data.reasoningText:
Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan the component decomposition and then implement everything.

## Component Plan: Settings Dashboard

### Component Tree
```
Settings                    (page — owns activeSection, orchestrates layout)
├── SettingsSidebar          (vertical nav tabs)
├── ProfileSettings          (profile editing section)
├── NotificationSettings     (notification prefs section)
├── SecuritySettings         (security section)
│   ├── ChangePasswordPanel  (expandable password change form)
│   └── ActiveSessionsTable  (sessions with revoke)
└── AppearanceSettings       (appearance section with live preview)
```

The Settings page will manage the active section state and pass it down to the sidebar, which handles navigation. Each settings section will use dependency injection to access the ISettingsService and manage its own data. I'll build them in order: starting with the service and models, then the sidebar, followed by each individual settings section, and finally composing everything together with the styling.

The namespace for all of this is `sv_59ff03f258a24ce2b692bad4433ffbeb`. I need to create the models file, all the Razor components for each section, and make sure the naming doesn't conflict—SecuritySettings as a component name should work fine since the record is just `SecuritySettings`.

```

csharp
// Models/SettingsModels.cs
namespace sv_59ff03f258a24ce2b692bad4433ffbeb;

public record ProfileSettings(string FirstName, string LastName, string Email, string PhoneNumber);
public record NotificationSettings(bool EmailNotifications, bool PushNotifications, bool SmsNotifications);
public record SecuritySettings(bool TwoFactorEnabled, DateTime LastPasswordChange);
public record AppearanceSettings(string Theme, string Language);

public interface ISettingsService
{
    Task<ProfileSettings> GetProfileSettingsAsync();
    Task UpdateProfileSettingsAsync(ProfileSettings settings);
    Task<NotificationSettings> GetNotificationSettingsAsync();
    Task UpdateNotificationSettingsAsync(NotificationSettings settings);
    Task<SecuritySettings> GetSecuritySettingsAsync();
    Task<AppearanceSettings> GetAppearanceSettingsAsync();
    Task UpdateAppearanceSettingsAsync(AppearanceSettings settings);
    Task ChangePasswordAsync(string currentPassword, string newPassword);
    Task<List<ActiveSession>> GetActiveSessionsAsync();
    Task RevokeSessionAsync(string sessionId);
}

public record ActiveSession(string SessionId, string DeviceInfo, DateTime LoginTime, DateTime LastActivity);
```

Now I'll create the sidebar component that displays the navigation menu for settings sections.

```razor
@* Components/Pages/Settings/SettingsSidebar.razor *@
<div class="settings-sidebar">
    <nav class="settings-nav">
        <a href="#profile" class="nav-item @(ActiveSection == "profile" ? "active" : "")">
            <span class="icon">👤</span> Profile
        </a>
        <a href="#notifications" class="nav-item @(ActiveSection == "notifications" ? "active" : "")">
            <span class="icon">🔔</span> Notifications
        </a>
        <a href="#security" class="nav-item @(ActiveSection == "security" ? "active" : "")">
            <span class="icon">🔒</span> Security
        </a>
        <a href="#appearance" class="nav-item @(ActiveSection == "appearance" ? "active" : "")">
            <span class="icon">🎨</span> Appearance
        </a>
    </nav>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string ActiveSection { get; set; } = "profile";
}
```

Now the profile settings component that handles name, email, and phone updates.

```razor
@* Components/Pages/Settings/ProfileSettings.razor *@
@inject ISettingsService SettingsService

<div class="settings-section">
    <h2>Profile Settings</h2>
    <form @onsubmit="HandleSubmit">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="firstName">First Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="firstName" @bind="profile.FirstName" class="form-control" />
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="lastName">Last Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="lastName" @bind="profile.LastName" class="form-control" />
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="email">Email</label>
            <input type="email" id="email" @bind="profile.Email" class="form-control" />
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="phone">Phone Number</label>
            <input type="tel" id="phone" @bind="profile.PhoneNumber" class="form-control" />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save Changes</button>
    </form>
</div>

@code {
    private ProfileSettings profile = new("", "", "", "");

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        profile = await SettingsService.GetProfileSettingsAsync();
    }

    private async Task HandleSubmit()
    {
        await SettingsService.UpdateProfileSettingsAsync(profile);
    }
}
```

Now the notifications settings component for managing email, push, and SMS preferences.

```

razor
@* Components/Pages/Settings/NotificationsSection.razor *@
@inject ISettingsService SettingsService

<div class="settings-section">
    <h2>Notification Preferences</h2>
    <div class="notification-options">
        <div class="checkbox-group">
            <input type="checkbox" id="emailNotif" @bind="notifications.EmailNotifications" />
            <label for="emailNotif">Email Notifications</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-group">
            <input type="checkbox" id="pushNotif" @bind="notifications.PushNotifications" />
            <label for="pushNotif">Push Notifications</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-group">
            <input type="checkbox" id="smsNotif" @bind="notifications.SmsNotifications" />
            <label for="smsNotif">SMS Notifications</label>
        </div>
    </div>
    <button @onclick="SaveNotifications" class="btn btn-primary">Save Preferences</button>
</div>

@code {
    private NotificationSettings notifications = new(false, false, false);

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        notifications = await SettingsService.GetNotificationSettingsAsync();
    }

    private async Task SaveNotifications()
    {
        await SettingsService.UpdateNotificationSettingsAsync(notifications);
    }
}
```

Now the security settings component with two-factor authentication toggle and password change functionality.

```razor
